<metadata>
  <!--
    Rules are the exceptions, not the norm: the generator handles the rest of the surface
    unaided. Every rule states what breaks without it, so an upgrade can re-check whether the
    upstream shape that motivated it still exists. The build log cannot tell a rule that still
    matches from a stale one - BG8A00 ("matched no nodes") is printed either way, see below - so
    every rule also says how to check it.
  -->

  <!--
    Response.Creator is a Kotlin companion-object CREATOR for Android's Parcelable plumbing whose
    generic signature defeats the generator: the emitted C# for the nested creator fails to
    compile against the projected Response type. Nothing user-facing is lost - Parcelable
    creators are called by the OS through reflection, never from C#. Carried over from the
    pre-rebuild sfmc-net-bindings-mobile repository, where it was needed for sfmcsdk 1.x; still
    present, and still needed, in 3.3.0: without the rule every target framework fails with
    CS0738, "'Response.Creator' does not implement interface member
    'IParcelableCreator.CreateFromParcel(Parcel?)'".

    How to re-check it on an upgrade. Do not go by the build log: the generator reports BG8A00
    ("matched no nodes") for this rule on every build, on 3.1.1 and 3.3.0 alike, although the
    rule does match. Compare the generator's input with its output instead -
    obj/Release/<tfm>/api.xml must contain the class and api.xml.fixed must not:

      xmllint -xpath "count(<the path below>)" obj/Release/<tfm>/api.xml        -> 1
      xmllint -xpath "count(<the path below>)" obj/Release/<tfm>/api.xml.fixed  -> 0
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.salesforce.marketingcloud.sfmcsdk.components.http']/class[@name='Response.Creator']" />
</metadata>
